executive=f'''<div class="prose"><span class="eyebrow">EXECUTIVE SUMMARY / SUBMISSION GUIDE</span><h1>Your GeoTIFF, ready to inspect.</h1><p class="lead">The file has been generated and independently re-opened. Download it directly—no conversion, editing, or model training is required.</p>{download_block()}<div class="notice"><strong>The blocked-holdout gate now passes for this file.</strong><p>The shipped configuration emits its mass fresh inside every held-out 20 km block and beats a uniform-random control at equal mass in all four folds — mean DTI 0.2507 vs 0.1212 (catalogue-density control 0.1771). That satisfies the standing promotion rule, so one of the three weekly slots may be spent on it. It is <em>not</em> a score forecast: the holdout truth is the published catalogue, not the hidden expert fault set.</p></div><p>The archived source-vector transfer arm and its preregistered follow-on test also failed to improve the fixed holdout, so they remain not-to-submit. H41 IDs are workstream-scoped; <a href="{REPO}/blob/main/research/hypothesis-id-registry.md">see the ID registry</a>. <a href="research.html#follow-on">Read the result and the remaining ranked hypotheses →</a></p>
<h2>Artifact identity</h2><p><strong>Filename</strong><br><code>{M['filename']}</code></p><p><strong>Unique submission name</strong><br><code>{M['submission_name']}</code></p><p><strong>Short note ({len(M['note'])} characters)</strong></p><div class="copybox"><code id="submission-note">{E(M['note'])}</code><button class="copy" data-copy="submission-note" type="button">Copy note</button></div><p class="fine">SHA-256: <code>{M['format']['sha256']}</code></p>
<section class="section"><h2>Submit the H42 file</h2><ol><li>Confirm the <strong>clean, spatially blocked comparison</strong> for this exact SHA-256 in the <a href="downloads/h42-gate.json">gate receipt</a>: candidate mean DTI 0.2507, worst fold 0.2423, uniform-random control 0.1212, catalogue-density control 0.1771. Require an improvement before spending one of the three weekly slots.</li><li>Download the single <code>.tif</code> using the button above. Do not upload the map PNG, HTML page, audit JSON, or a renamed document.</li><li>Sign in to <a href="https://www.drivendata.org/competitions/306/competition-doe-gems/">DrivenData’s GEMS competition</a>, confirm eligibility and accept the official rules using your own account.</li><li>Open <strong>New submission</strong>. Under <strong>File to submit</strong>, choose the downloaded GeoTIFF. Use the unique name in your internal tracker and paste the short note into <strong>Note (optional)</strong>.</li><li>Submit only after the gate passes. Wait for the portal’s validation and score. Record the exact file hash, submission ID, note, and organizer-reported score. A local validator cannot guarantee portal acceptance.</li><li>Select one final submission for both prize rounds by the official deadline. Disclose AI assistance in the required narrative; eligibility and certifications must be completed by the participant.</li></ol><p>These steps follow the <a href="{PROBLEM}#submission-format">format specification</a> and <a href="https://docs.nlr.gov/docs/fy26osti/96647.pdf">official rules, §§3.2–3.5</a>.</p></section>
<section class="section"><h2>Why this file avoids the range error</h2><p>Every one of its 12,279,160 stored values is finite, with minimum {M['format']['min']:.0f} and maximum {M['format']['max']:.0f}. There is no negative sentinel or NaN-valued nodata tag. Outside-footprint cells contain numeric zero <em>and</em> are null through an internal GeoTIFF mask matching the template. This reconciles the published null-outside requirement with safe numerical values.</p><p>This is the <strong>new H42 submission</strong> (<code>{M['submission_name']}</code>), not the archived H41 file. The exact cause of your earlier portal error is unknown without the rejected bytes. Out-of-range sentinel values are one possible cause; NaN alone is not proven to be the cause. We verified the current file rather than guessing about the old one.</p></section>
<section class="section"><h2>Secondary research artifacts from the parallel bimodal-lattice/H42 session</h2><p>The other H42 lineage ships <code>{BLPF}</code> (unique name <code>{E(BL['submission_name'])}</code>) and <code>{BLSF}</code> as labeled research. Both store values exactly 0.0 or 1.0 — the “[0,1]” rejection class is impossible by construction — with 0 cells ≤200 m from the published catalogue, but both failed their preregistered promotion gates. <strong>Not for submission.</strong> Their note, for trackers: {E(BL['note'])}</p><p><a href="{REPO}/blob/main/research/hypotheses-h42.md">Full preregistration and outcome log →</a> · <a href="research.html#h42-bimodal-lattice">Measured tables →</a></p></section>
<section class="section"><h2>Rebuild rather than copy</h2><pre><code>bash scripts/download_competition_data.sh
.venv/bin/python scripts/prepare_data.py
.venv/bin/python scripts/run_pipeline.py
.venv/bin/python scripts/build_site.py</code></pre><p><a href="{REPO}/actions/workflows/reproduce.yml">Run the reproducibility workflow</a> or use the setup commands in the README. The geometry-only model is CPU-based; it does not require a GPU. Rebuilding identical inputs reproduces the same scientific hypothesis, not an artificial “new” submission made by renaming it. Cross-run pixel values are audited to an absolute tolerance of 64 float32 epsilons (about 0.00000763); the exact grid, valid mask, and outside-footprint encoding must also match. Exact file hashes still identify the specific delivered bytes.</p></section>
<section class="section"><h2>Supplemental raster-derived variant (not this guide’s primary file)</h2><p>The repository also preserves <strong>H41-A-R</strong>, a distinct raster-input implementation from PR #8. It is separate from the main source-vector H41-A above. H41-A-R has no eligible support in {ALT_UNSUPPORTED_FOLDS}/4 held-out interiors; its candidate DTI is null/unevaluable and its slot gate is closed. <a href="h41a-raster-variant.html">Review its evidence</a> or <a href="{ALT_DOWNLOAD}" download>download that research GeoTIFF</a>. Those two H41 candidates remain not-to-submit: their arms measured 0.0 on the same holdout that the H42 file above passes. Only the H42 file at the top of this page is slot-eligible.</p></section></div>'''
