sources_html=f'''<span class="eyebrow">SOURCE REGISTER / MANUAL REVIEW</span><h1>Evidence you can follow.</h1><p class="lead">Official observations, owner-reported history, and our measured results are separate evidence classes. Links are not a substitute for testing a geological hypothesis.</p>{table(['ID / source','Evidence class','Verified scope'],[[f'<a href="{url}">{id} · {E(title)}</a>',E(kind),E(claim)] for id,title,url,kind,claim in sources])}<section class="section"><h2>Input lineage</h2><p>Official INGENIOUS vector bytes were fetched on a GitHub runner, archive-tested and checksum-pinned. The archive and field definitions are preserved under <code>data/official/</code>. Core rasters came from owner mirrors pinned to commits and SHA-256 in <a href="{REPO}/blob/main/research/input-receipt.json">the input receipt</a>. Hash equality proves mirror integrity, not organizer authentication. No prior prediction raster enters the structural model.</p><p>The <a href="downloads/classified-traces.csv">trace table</a> preserves the original source fields, including slip sense, and distinguishes geometric family from measured kinematics. The <a href="downloads/corridors-utm11.geojson">corridor GeoJSON</a> is explicitly projected UTM11, not RFC 7946 longitude/latitude; use QGIS with EPSG:32611.</p></section><section class="section"><h2>39 related sites, audited</h2><p>All 39 supplied website source files were retrieved through the GitHub contents API and inspected for primary-download, holdout, and score claims. This is a source-level audit, not an exhaustive rerun of every project or verification of every claimed score. Placeholders 40–44 in the brief have no supplied site or result.</p><p><a href="related-sites.json">Complete source hashes and claim excerpts (JSON)</a> · <a href="score-ledger.csv">All submission scores reported in the brief (CSV)</a></p>{table(['Project','Source audit','Evidence class'],[[f'<a href="{r["url"]}">{E(r["repo"])}</a>',E(r['status']),'Owner-authored; no organizer artifact receipt'] for r in related])}</section><section class="section"><h2>Refresh status</h2><p id="source-feed" aria-live="polite">{source_feed_fallback()}<a href="{LEADER}">Open official leaderboard ↗</a> · <a href="https://www.drivendata.org/termsofuse/">Terms of Use ↗</a></p><p><a href="source-feed.json">Timestamped feed JSON</a> · <a href="{REPO}/actions/workflows/site.yml">Source-refresh and Pages run history</a></p><p>The daily workflow checks only non-competition official sources and never fetches the DrivenData site. Failed availability probes are published with their errors and do not become claims about source outage or freshness. This site does not collect logins, use hidden labels, or upload to DrivenData.</p></section>'''
